# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .dockerignore — deny-all + explicit allowlist (leak-proof build context)
#
# Anything NOT allowlisted below is excluded from the build context, so the
# image can never carry local secrets or client configs even if a future
# Dockerfile COPY adds a path. Those live outside the image and are
# bind-mounted at runtime by services/pipeline/compose.yaml instead:
#   .env*           secrets, root + services/            → never included
#   clients/*.yml   real client configs                  → never included
#   .git/, data/    repo history + local data            → never included
#   target/, logs/  build output + logs                  → never included
#   caches, .venv   local tooling/caches                 → never included
#   docs/           documentation (not needed to build)  → never included
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Deny everything ──
*

# ── Allowlist (builder stage needs exactly these) ──
!Dockerfile
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/
